        "original_id": "a4762306-eb4d-56ad-9705-efc552e46489",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Waputik Mountains\n- People: George M. Dawson\n- Animals: Mountain goat, Oreamnos americanus\n- Languages and Concepts: Stoney Indian word “waputik”, etymology\n\nFacts:\n- In 1884, George M. Dawson named the Waputik Mountains.\n- In 1884, George M. Dawson stated that “waputik” is the Stoney Indian word for “white goat.”\n- The mountain goat is also known as the Rocky Mountain goat.\n- The mountain goat has the scientific name Oreamnos americanus.\n- The mountain goat is a large hoofed mammal endemic to North America.",
